From: Rasheed <99349713+gitRasheed@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 23:42:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 25/61] NNS.ARMA.optim: pass negative.values to the linear
 search

The two NNS.ARMA calls of the lin stage (parallel and sequential) did not
pass negative.values, so the linear candidates were scored with
forecasts clipped at 0 even when the user (or auto-detection) allowed
negative values. The nonlin, both and final stages do pass it, so the
search scored a different model from the one it fitted.

Before -> after (work/TS/data/down.csv, a positive series trending below
0, h = 12, seasonal.factor = c(3,6,12,24), negative.values = TRUE):
  method lin,  periods 12, obj.fn 0.1574, results -2.425 -2.429 -1.199 1.342
  method both, periods 12, obj.fn 0.1994, results -1.183 -2.350 -0.921 0.918
Series without negative values are unchanged (AirPassengers configs
identical).
---
 R/ARMA_optim.R | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/R/ARMA_optim.R b/R/ARMA_optim.R
index 5565450..a086f27 100644
--- a/R/ARMA_optim.R
+++ b/R/ARMA_optim.R
@@ -210,7 +210,8 @@ NNS.ARMA.optim <- function(variable,
               h = h_eval,
               seasonal.factor = seasonal.combs[[i]][, k],
               method = "lin",
-              plot = FALSE
+              plot = FALSE,
+              negative.values = negative.values
             )
             eval(obj.fn)
           })
@@ -223,7 +224,8 @@ NNS.ARMA.optim <- function(variable,
               h = h_eval,
               seasonal.factor = seasonal.combs[[i]][, k],
               method = "lin",
-              plot = FALSE
+              plot = FALSE,
+              negative.values = negative.values
             )
             eval(obj.fn)
           })
